One test failure — not an engine bug but a bug in my test: on non-flap ticks, gravity is added to the input `vy` first, so starting from `vy=18` gives `vy=36`. To land exactly on the floor boundary, the input needs to be `vy=0`:
DONE. `test_flapsim.py` has 18 tests, all passing:

- **Physics clamps** (5): flap sets `vy` rather than adding, gravity clamps at `VY_MAX`, soft ceiling zeroes vy, floor clamps y and kills without zeroing vy, exact floor boundary (`y + BIRD_H == FIELD_H`) survives.
- **LCG/world** (4): `lcg` known values and range, spawn advances the LCG exactly once and derives `gap_top` from the advanced state, spawn gating on `t % SPAWN_EVERY`, cull boundary at `x + PIPE_W == 0`.
- **AABB edges** (4): half-open touching edges don't overlap, pipe right edge exactly at `BIRD_X` no hit, bird top/bottom exactly on gap edges survives, one centi-unit outside hits.
- **Clean-glide bonus** (2): level pass scores 2 per pipe (seed 7 / "0010" → 8), a hand-computed free-fall scenario passes pipe 0 at `vy=180 > GLIDE_VY` and scores exactly 1.
- **Per-tick order** (3): floor kill landing exactly on a pass tick scores nothing (dead bird, score-after-collision), ceiling-stuck run dies at the first post-scroll overlap pinning spawn+scroll to their own tick (`ticks_run=41`, would be 42 if either lagged), and state-dict keys without powerups.

The one failure during development was a bug in my test expectation (forgot gravity applies before the floor check), not the engine — fixed, and `--selfcheck` still reports all six OK.

